<title>UK: Leeds Utd gets funds to expand Elland Road.</title>
<headline>Leeds Utd gets funds to expand Elland Road.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>British football club Leeds United will expand its Elland Road stadium following a stock placing which raised 5.7 million stg, parent company Caspian Group Plc said on Monday.</p>
<p>Caspian said it placed 13.56 million new ordinary shares with two unnamed institutions at 42p per share.</p>
<p>&quot;It is intended that the proceeds will be applied towards a further fit-out and extension of the east stand at Elland Road football stadium,&quot; Caspian said in a statement.</p>
<p>The company said it would apply to the London Stock Exchange to admit the new shares to the official list.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
